---
title: Spiced Lamb Pies
---

Heat the @olive oil{2%tbsp} in a #sauté pan{}.
Add the @ground lamb{12%oz}, season with @salt and @pepper.
Stir over medium-high heat, until evenly browned. 
With a slotted spoon, transfer to a bowl. 

Reduce the heat to medium, and pour off all but 2 tablespoons of the fat. 
Add the @garlic cloves{3}(finely chopped) and @fresh ginger{1/2%inch}(finely chopped) and cook for 30 seconds. 
Add the @onion{1}(finely chopped) and stir until soft. 

Add the @ground coriander{1/2%tsp}, @ground cumin{1/4%tsp}, @ground turmeric{1/4%tsp},
@cayenne pepper{pinch}, @tomatoes{2}(peeled, seeded, and chopped), and cooked lamb.
Cover and cook for ~{10%minutes}, until thickened.

Remove the pan from the heat.
Stir in the @cilantro{5%sprigs}(fresh, chopped) and taste for seasoning.
Let the filling cool, then taste again: it should be well seasoned, so adjust if necessary.

Prepare a batch of dough (unbaked) from the @./Breads/Traditional_Pita_Breads{1} recipe.
Cut the dough in half.
Shape 1 piece into a cylinder about 2" in diameter.
Cut into 6 pieces, and cover.
Repeat with the remaining dough.

Shape a piece of dough into a ball.
With a #rolling pin{}, roll into a 4" round.
Spoon some of the lamb into the center of the round, leaving a 1" border.

Lift the dough up and over the filling, to form a triangular parcel.
Pinch the edges with your fingers to seal.
Place the pie on a #baking sheet{}.
Repeat to shape and fill the remaining dough.

Cover the pies with a kitchen towel, and let rise in a warm place until puffed, about ~{20%minutes}.

Meanwhile, preheat the oven to 450°F.
Bake for ~{10-15%minutes} until golden brown.

Serve warm from the oven with a spoonful of #Greek yogurt{}(optional) on the side, if you like.
